# Always ship to production

After any substantive file change in this repo, **do not wait to be asked**:

1. `git add` (scoped; never secrets / `.env`)
2. `git commit` with a clear why-focused message
3. `git push origin main` (production branch)

## Production = main

- Default delivery is **`main`** → Vercel Production.
- Do not leave finished work only on a feature/Dependabot/preview branch.
- Prefer fixing on `main` over long-lived PR-only deploys unless the user asks for a PR.

## Skip only when

- Read-only session (no file changes)
- User says **do not commit**, **do not push**, or **local only**
- Working tree is clean after your work

## Safety

- No force-push to `main`
- No `--no-verify` unless explicitly requested
- No committing secrets
- Fix broken builds before push when the change is deploy-bound
